message: "If you use this software or data, please cite the article and this archive."
title: "semantic-burstiness-texts: code and data for 'Semantic burstiness across principal directions of textual variation'"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-19
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mirko-degli-esposti/semantic-burstiness-pca"
authors:
  - family-names: Degli Esposti
    given-names: Mirko
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0316-3449"
    affiliation: "Department of Physics and Astronomy, University of Bologna, Italy"
  - family-names: Montemurro
    given-names: Marcelo A.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0893-8530"
    affiliation: "School of Mathematics and Statistics, The Open University, United Kingdom"
keywords:
  - long-range correlations
  - burstiness
  - word embeddings
  - principal component analysis
  - surrogate data
abstract: >-
  Code, corpus and result tables for the article. Literary and scientific
  texts are mapped token by token onto GloVe word-embedding trajectories;
  PCA identifies text-specific directions of semantic variation, and the
  burstiness of threshold-crossing events along each component is compared
  with a word-shuffled null and a Zipf-preserving fractional-Gaussian-noise
  surrogate.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "A Zipf-preserving, long-range correlated surrogate for written language and other symbolic sequences"
    authors:
      - family-names: Montemurro
        given-names: Marcelo A.
      - family-names: Degli Esposti
        given-names: Mirko
    journal: "Physica A: Statistical Mechanics and its Applications"
    volume: 683
    start: 131227
    year: 2026
    doi: 10.1016/j.physa.2025.131227
